{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.support_eq_mpi_mul_of_support_ne_zero_of_ledger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.support_eq_mpi_mul_of_support_ne_zero_of_ledger","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L190-L198","doc":"Conditional corollary: a nonzero bond-channel scale is necessarily\n`m_π`-valued — the categorical face of the Yukawa-range statement (the\nbond length unit is `ℏc/(m_π·Q(q₀))`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.support_eq_ite_of_ledger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.support_eq_ite_of_ledger","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L173-L188","doc":"Conditional factoring: the bond-channel support of every class is either\nzero or the CAL-3 value `m_π·Q(cal3)` — the bond length unit factors\nthrough the CAL-3 class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.eq_cal3_of_support_ne_zero_of_ledger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.eq_cal3_of_support_ne_zero_of_ledger","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L162-L171","doc":"**Uniqueness (conditional on the ledger identification).**  CAL-3 is the\nunique calibration class with (possibly) nonzero support on the Vol = 0\nbond channel: any class with nonzero bond-channel support is CAL-3.\nThis is the 0-bit class selection of the audit's finding (a). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.support_cal2_eq_zero_of_ledger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.support_cal2_eq_zero_of_ledger","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L156-L160","doc":"Conditional on the ledger identification: CAL-2's bond-channel support\nvanishes identically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.support_cal1_eq_zero_of_ledger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.support_cal1_eq_zero_of_ledger","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L150-L154","doc":"Conditional on the ledger identification: CAL-1's bond-channel support\nvanishes identically (`m_e·Vol(Hopf)·Q = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BindingVolumeLedger.support_cal3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BindingVolumeLedger.support_cal3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L143-L143","doc":"CAL-3 supports the bond channel through the meson scale. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BindingVolumeLedger.support_cal2_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BindingVolumeLedger.support_cal2_eq","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L141-L141","doc":"CAL-2 supports the bond channel only through the W-plane term (its\nmodulus q₀ being dimensionless). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BindingVolumeLedger.support_cal1_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BindingVolumeLedger.support_cal1_eq","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L138-L138","doc":"CAL-1 supports the bond channel only through the W-plane term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BindingVolumeLedger.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BindingVolumeLedger.mk","kind":"ctor","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L135-L135","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BindingVolumeLedger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BindingVolumeLedger","kind":"class","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L118-L144","doc":"**Conditional carrier (§3b-cond) — the `B = m_e·Vol` ledger\nidentification.**  The fields axiomatise the HYPOTHESES of the\nclass-selection argument, not its conclusion: the W-plane classes\n(CAL-1, CAL-2) enter per-link binding only through the W-plane term\n`m_e·Vol·Q` (the per-link volume-conjecture instances of the\nbinding-scale ledger), and CAL-3 only through the meson scale `m_π`\ntimes a dimensionless factor.  The vanishing and uniqueness statements\nare DERIVED from these fields together with `volBond_eq_zero` — the\nclass does not carry them.\n\nThis is a primary conjecture carrier: NO instance is declared anywhere\n(an unproved premise is honestly represented by a content-bearing class\nwith no instance; fabricating an instance would launder the ledger\nidentification, AGENTS.md §Axiomatization is NOT a Proof).\n\n-- @conjecture: primary\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] docs/coordination/binding-scale-is-hyperbolic-volume.md ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.wPlaneTerm_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.wPlaneTerm_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L109-L114","doc":"**Proved outright:** the W-plane term is identically zero on the bond\nchannel, for every class's q₀-factor — `m_e·Vol(Hopf)·Q = 0` since\n`Vol(Hopf) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.wPlaneTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.wPlaneTerm","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L106-L107","doc":"The W-plane per-link term on the bond channel: `m_e·Vol(bond)·Q(c)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.volBond_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.volBond_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L100-L100","doc":"Geometric input: `Vol(Hopf) = 0` (the Hopf complement is\nnon-hyperbolic). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.support","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L97-L97","doc":"Dimensionful support of each calibration class on the bond channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.volBond","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.volBond","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L95-L95","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the bond (Hopf, 2-body) channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.qFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.qFactor","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L93-L93","doc":"Dimensionless q₀-rational factor attached to each class — CAL-2's\nentire contribution enters through such factors (q₀ is dimensionless,\nso CAL-2 carries no length scale of its own). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.mpi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.mpi","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L89-L89","doc":"CAL-3 scale `m_π` (the orthogonal meson scale). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.me","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.me","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L87-L87","doc":"CAL-1 scale `m_e` (the W-plane scale / dimensional unit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.BondChannelModel","kind":"structure","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L79-L100","doc":"Small algebraic model of the three calibration classes and their\nlength-scale support on the inter-nucleon bond channel.  The field\n`volBond_eq_zero` records the geometric input: the bond channel is the\n2-body Hopf class, whose complement is non-hyperbolic, `Vol(Hopf) = 0`\n(SnapPy-verified; ledger\n`docs/coordination/binding-scale-is-hyperbolic-volume.md`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.wplane_term_eq_zero_of_vol_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.wplane_term_eq_zero_of_vol_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L69-L77","doc":"**The W-plane term vanishes on `Vol = 0` channels.**  The per-link\nW-plane contribution is `m_e·Vol(K)·Q` with `Q` a dimensionless\nq₀-factor; on a channel of vanishing hyperbolic volume it is zero\nidentically — for every scale `m_e` and every factor `Q`.  Trivial\nmultiplication, structurally load-bearing: this is the annihilation\nstep (a2) of the class-selection argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.instDecidableEqCalClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.instDecidableEqCalClass","kind":"instance","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.CalClass.cal3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.CalClass.cal3","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L62-L64","doc":"CAL-3: the pion-sector bar-even channel `P_avg^π` / meson scale `m_π` — the\ncohomologically orthogonal `Vol(Hopf) = 0` class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.CalClass.cal2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.CalClass.cal2","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L59-L61","doc":"CAL-2: the β-decay width `P_skew^β`, numerically pinned via `m_μ/m_e` — the\nW-plane *modulus* `q₀`, a dimensionless quantity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.CalClass.cal1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.CalClass.cal1","kind":"ctor","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L57-L58","doc":"CAL-1: the leptonic mass scale `m_e` — the W-plane *scale*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.CalClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BondChannelClassSelection.CalClass","kind":"inductive","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BondChannelClassSelection.lean#L54-L65","doc":"The three calibration classes of the canonical triple (the ideal\nmathematical calibrations; AGENTS.md cheat-sheet table). ","signatureChunk":0}]}